[%cachewrite 1647] The g-file is fully open, so the queen on g3 checks the king
directly. The main options: - **Qh7-g7 to block**: this offers a queen trade.
Black is currently up a piece for a pawn (Black has bishop and knight, White
has only a knight). Trading queens simplifies into an endgame a piece up. -
**Kh8**: the king stays with the queen on the h-file. White can then use Qh4
and Nh4 to harass. It is more complicated. - **Kf7**: the king gets too
exposed. After Qg7, if White plays Qxg7+, then Kxg7 gives a clean endgame. If
White tries Nh4 to hit the bishop on f5, Black can play Qxg3 fxg3 and then move
the bishop to safety. Black stays a piece up either way. } 25. Qf4 Bxh3 {
